   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "ous popular force behind the pressure that is being exerted upon the Democratic party for federal action upon this question. This demonstration will be the culmination of the picket siege begun at the time of the President's last refusal to act.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p7#xywh=6011,7965,1677,952"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p7/text/r17",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "Down all the history of democracy people have established their rights by showing thejr strength to the men in power. It is no new move for the disfranchised to march upon parliaments and surround heads of governments to remind them that they are waiting for justice. Let women, then, join in a deputation of such size that it will move the President and the Democratic party to recognize the strength as they have recognized the justice of their demand.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p7#xywh=6005,8939,1672,1602"
